  "problem": "Solve the inequality $-(0.75)^{2-3x}<(0.98)^{3x-1}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since $(0.98)^{3x-1}$ is always positive and $-(0.75)^{2-3x}$ is always negative, we always have\n\n$$\n-(0.75)^{2-3x}<(0.98)^{3x-1}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the given inequality is satisfied by all real values of $x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-\\infty <x<\\infty \n$$",
